<item><title>CAF names Mané and Gueye among five African player finalists</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/sn/caf-names-mane-and-gueye-among-five-african-player-finalists-484c3b/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/sn/caf-names-mane-and-gueye-among-five-african-player-finalists-484c3b/</guid><category>Senegal</category><description>Senegal has two contenders, while Morocco leads with three; the winner will be announced at the CAF Awards in Lagos on 2 December.</description><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 09:03:30 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/sn.jpg" length="32606" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/sn.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Senegal seminar examines management of borders with Gambia and Guinea-Bissau</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/sn/senegal-seminar-examines-management-of-borders-with-gambia-12f435/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/sn/senegal-seminar-examines-management-of-borders-with-gambia-12f435/</guid><category>Senegal</category><description>Researchers and specialists met in Ziguinchor to discuss how land and maritime boundaries can support peace and cooperation among the three countries.</description><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 08:26:52 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/sn.jpg" length="32606" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/sn.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
